This model has lower accuracy (61.5%) but is more useful for the stated goal. 
It caught 20 of the 22 rainy hours (rain recall 0.91) and missed only 2, which is a large improvement over KNN.
The cost is 35 false alarms (dry hours predicted as rain), so rain precision is only 0.36 and dry-hour recall falls to 0.53. 
The rain F1 of 0.52 and macro F1 of 0.60 are both clearly better than KNN's. 
The pattern, high recall with low precision, is what you get when the model is pushed to favor the rare class.
An person should understand that accuracy dropped on purpose: the model trades false alarms for catching rain, which is the right trade if missing rain is the costly mistake.

